Apply fixes for PENDING metadata issues

Usage: fix [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --corrupted
          Fix corrupted TPE2 issues

      --orphans
          Fix orphan artist issues (delete them)

      --duplicates
          Fix duplicate artist issues (merge B into A)

      --missing
          Fix missing metadata issues

      --revert
          Revert already-applied fixes instead of applying new ones

      --mode <MODE>
          Revert mode

          Possible values:
          - undo:          Back to DETECTED - the issue is queued again next time it's picked up
          - undo-resolved: Stays RESOLVED - the file/DB change is undone, the issue is not re-queued
          
          [default: undo]

      --dry-run
          Print what would be fixed without writing files or the database

      --assign-artist
          Say which artist a release belongs to: write this MusicBrainz artist id (--mbid) into the album-artist id of every file of --release or --folder, then re-index them. For two artists sharing a name, and for a download being merged for a known artist

      --mbid <MBID>
          With --assign-artist: the MusicBrainz artist id to write

      --release <RELEASE>
          With --assign-artist: the LocalRelease id whose files to write

      --folder <FOLDER>
          With --assign-artist: a folder (relative to MUSIC_DIR, or absolute) whose audio files to write

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
